  "prediction": "**Implementing Telework to Reduce Office Space: Challenges and Opportunities**\n\nThe Government Accountability Office (GAO) conducted a study to examine how civilian Chief Financial Officer (CFO) Act agencies use telework to reduce office space and increase efficiency. The study found that most agencies have a telework program in place, but many face challenges in using telework as a strategic space-planning tool.\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n*   23 civilian CFO Act agencies reported using telework to reduce or use space more efficiently, with 15 agencies incorporating telework into their space-planning policies and procedures.\n*   Agencies reported using telework to reduce space, lower real estate costs, and reduce the size of individual workstations.\n*   The study identified three major planning challenges agencies face with using telework to reduce space: human capital issues, suitability of telework to mission work requirements, and difficulty measuring cost savings.\n*   Nearly two-thirds of agencies reported that they would like guidance on using telework programs or other alternatives to meet federal goals of reducing space or using space more efficiently.\n\n**Recommendations:**\n\nThe GAO made two recommendations to the General Services Administration (GSA):\n\n1.  Ensure that the appropriate GSA offices develop guidance on how agencies can use telework as a strategic space-planning tool for reducing and optimizing office space efficiency.\n2.  Ensure that the appropriate GSA offices complete the Workplace Investment and Feasibility Tool and make it available to federal agencies for use in assessing the benefits and costs of telework to achieve office space efficiencies.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe study highlights the potential benefits of using telework to reduce office space and increase efficiency, but also identifies challenges that agencies face in implementing this strategy. The GAO's recommendations aim to provide guidance and support to agencies in using telework as a strategic space-planning tool.",
